{"BlockedEmail.should_block? increments match_count and updates last_match_at during validation, causing stats to be inflated when user records fail to save due to other validation errors or when valid? is called multiple times": 0.8481826782226562, "The regex in email_in_restriction_setting? is missing an end-of-string anchor ($\\z), allowing emails like user@company.com.evil.org to incorrectly match whitelist entry for company.com": 0.7860397100448608, "BlockedEmail.should_block? uses case-sensitive comparison on PostgreSQL, allowing users to bypass email blocks by using different letter casing (e.g., SPAM@example.com bypasses block on spam@example.com)": 0.8623487949371338}